implementationPlan.description:
REUSE THE SLICE-2 SEAM (read-only). Sibling slice task-091c93db is DONE and established the pattern; read packages/runner/src/recovery-inventory/ before designing anything, and match it rather than inventing a second shape.

THE REGISTRY SEAM, from the contract slice: an enumerator is RecoveryInventoryEnumerator = (context: RecoveryInventoryEnumerationContext) => unknown. It returns exactly one of three shapes, validated by readPortResult and typed RecoveryInventoryPortReading:
  { status: "ENUMERATED", items, complete, negativeProofDigest }
  { status: "UNAVAILABLE" }
  { status: "UNSUPPORTED" }
THE ENUMERATOR NEVER MINTS A COVERAGE CODE. collectRecoveryInventory maps the reading to a coverage proof carrying RECOVERY_INVENTORY_COVERAGE_UNKNOWN, layer INVENTORY_ADAPTER and one RecoveryInventoryUnknownReason. So DoD 3 must be asserted END TO END through collectRecoveryInventory, never by unit-testing a private mapping helper.

*** DO NOT EDIT THE SLICE-1 AGGREGATE. *** createRecoveryInventoryRegistry takes an immutable caller-supplied tuple and its doc comment refuses a module-global because it "would let a sibling adapter slice change this aggregate's behaviour by importing it." You are that sibling slice. Export a RecoveryInventoryRegistration constant per class; tests compose their own registry. Zero changes to recovery-inventory.ts.

THIS SLICE OWNS EXACTLY TWO CLASSES: GIT_INTEGRATION_ON_DISK and ARTIFACT_OBJECT_STAGING. PROVIDER_PROCESS_LAUNCH_LOCK and WORKSPACE belong to slice 2 — already DONE, do not touch them.

The reason vocabulary already covers every DoD 3 case — invent nothing: ENUMERATOR_UNREGISTERED, ENUMERATOR_UNAVAILABLE, ENUMERATOR_FAILED, CAPABILITY_UNSUPPORTED, RESULT_MALFORMED, RESULT_TRUNCATED, RESULT_OVER_LIMIT, NEGATIVE_PROOF_MISSING, ITEM_REJECTED. Duplicate identity has its own code, RECOVERY_INVENTORY_EXTERNAL_IDENTITY_DUPLICATE. Consume identityKey and readInventoryItem from recovery-inventory-shape.ts rather than rebuilding them.
